<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt; text-indent: -18pt;">(1)&#160;&#160;&#160;The Company&#8217;s executive compensation program consists of both fixed base salaries and discretionary bonuses in the form of cash payments and restricted stock awards under the 2019 Equity Incentive Plan. Allocation of the cash payments and restricted stock awards is determined by the award recipients, provided that the cash payments may not be more than 50 percent of each total award. For additional information see &#8220;&#8212; Equity Incentive Plan&#8221; below.</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt; text-indent: -18pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;text-indent:-18pt;">(2)&#160;&#160;&#160;No restricted stock awards were granted for 2024. Restricted stock awards for 2025 were as follows: Mr. Dick &#8211; $532,500 (23,511 shares); Mr. Hersiburane -- $189,450 (8,367 shares); and Mr. Vari -- $162,000 (7,155 shares). Reflects aggregate grant date fair value of stock awards based upon the stock price on the date of the award in accordance with FASB ASC Topic 718. The restricted stock awards vest one-third after one year and one-third annually thereafter during periods of continued service by the award recipients until the awards are fully earned. The awards vest immediately upon a change in control transaction.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;text-indent:-18pt;">(3)&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of matching contributions under the Retirement Plan and dividends received on restricted stock awards.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<div class="PGBK" style="width: 100%; margin-left: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt">
<div class="PGFTR" style="text-align: center; width: 100%">
<div class="hf-row">
<div class="hf-cell PGNUM">24</div>
</div>
</div>

<hr style="PAGE-BREAK-AFTER: always; border: none; width: 100%; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000"/>
<div class="PGHDR" style="text-align: left; width: 100%">
<div class="hf-row">
<div class="hf-cell TOCLink">&#160;</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;text-indent:-18pt;">(4)&#160;&#160;&#160;In November 2025, the Company announced the planned retirement of Thomas J. Chmelik as Chief Financial Officer, effective as of December 31, 2025. Mr. Chmelik will continue to serve the Company and the Bank from January 1, 2026, through December 31, 2027, as Senior Executive Vice President and Secretary. In December 2025, the Company entered into a new employment agreement with Mr. Chmelik which replaced and superseded his prior employment agreement. Mr. Chmelik will also continue to serve as a member of the boards of directors of the Company and the Bank with terms expiring in 2027.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;text-indent:-18pt;">(5)&#160;&#160;In December 2025, the Company announced that Richard A. Vari would become Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer of the Company and the Bank, effective January 1, 2026. From July 2025 to December 31, 2025, he served as Chief Financial Officer of the Bank and was Chief Accounting Officer and Senior Vice President of the Company and the Bank from 2019 to July 2025.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The Compensation Committee of the Company&#8217;s Board of Directors has a policy governing the dispensation of incentive compensation for Named Executive Officers. To assist in this determination, the Compensation Committee engages an independent compensation consultant to compare the Company&#8217;s compensation and incentive strategy to ensure that it aligns with comparable peer banks. Mr. Dick has a target bonus of 125% of base compensation. Messrs. Hersiburane and Vari have target bonuses of 70% of base compensation.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The Compensation Committee uses quantitative/qualitative metrics in its calculation of three incentive targets. The incentive targets are: (1) Company return-on-average assets, (2) Company non-performing assets to total assets, and (3) Bank total common equity to risk-based capital after applying the &#8220;worst-case&#8221; loss results from the Company&#8217;s internal stress-test model.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">Each year, the Compensation Committee approves a value for each incentive target, which may be higher than those calculated within the annual budget. Targets are binary and do not change during the year, nor does the respective weighting for each incentive target. For 2025, two of the three incentive targets were met, and one incentive target was missed. The Named Executive Officers received bonuses for the two that were met. The Named Executive Officers elected to receive their 2025 incentive compensation as 100% restricted shares vesting evenly over a three-year period.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><b>Outstanding Equity Awards at Fiscal 2025 Year-End</b></p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The table below includes information with respect to all unvested restricted stock awards held by the named executive officers at December 31, 2025.</p>

